{"id":"CON-31","class":"contract","severity":"advisory","file":"src/ui/views/order-form.js","line":160,"what_breaks":"F-33 is not closed although commit f19ef9e says it is. The app now supplies `today`, but nothing in src reads it. The only live clock is still `deps.now`, called from the view.","requirement":"R-06","rule":"CP-07","evidence":"ADR-003 line 31: '`deps` carries what the outside supplies, `newId` and `today`'. Code: order-form.js:160 `todayIso(deps.now)`; main.js:74 '`now` stays for views that still read the clock'; main.js:77 `now: () =&gt; Date.now(),`. A grep for deps.today under src/ finds nothing. Commit f19ef9e: 'F-16, F-21, F-33, F-36, F-23..F-27 already closed in shared files'.","proven":true},
{"id":"CON-32","class":"contract","severity":"advisory","file":"src/ui/views/order-form.js","line":199,"what_breaks":"F-36 is not closed for the order form. It calls commit without a hash and then navigates itself, so the one write path of ADR-003 is still split. The target can be computed from result.data before the commit, as customer-form.js does with its own target.","requirement":"R-21","rule":"LY-08","evidence":"ADR-003 line 32: '`commit` calls `storage.save(result.data)`; only when that succeeds does it replace the state, navigate and render.' Code: order-form.js:199 `const saved = commit(result.data);`, then :204-205 `state.form = null; location.hash = savedHash(route, result.data);`. F-36's evidence named this exact call site (order-form.js:203). customer-form.js:110 uses `commit(result.data, where.saved)`. Commit f19ef9e lists F-36 as 'already closed in shared files'.","proven":true},
{"id":"CON-33","class":"contract","severity":"advisory","file":"src/ui/views/order-form.js","line":201,"what_breaks":"F-15 is fixed only on the customer form. After a failed storage save on the order form, focus still moves to the banner, not to Save.","requirement":"R-21","evidence":"UI-SPEC line 502: 'Failed Save, storage | stays on Save, ready to retry'. Code: order-form.js:201 `showBanner(saved.code);` then `return;`, and main.js:121 `return setBanner(region, bannerFor(code)).focus();`. F-15's what_breaks says 'the customer or order form' and its evidence names order-form.js:199. customer-form.js:113 got `form.querySelector('[type=\"submit\"]').focus();`; order-form.js did not. F-15 was routed to S11 only, so S14 never received it.","proven":true},
{"id":"CON-34","class":"contract","severity":"advisory","file":"src/ui/views/order-list.js","line":105,"what_breaks":"F-34 is fixed in one of the three views. order-list.js and order-view.js still read the browser locale themselves, and they ignore the `locale` the composition root now passes.","requirement":"R-16","rule":"LY-10","evidence":"ADR-006 line 24: 'The locale is `navigator.language`, read once in `src/ui/main.js` and passed as an argument'. Code: order-list.js:105 and order-view.js:199 `const locale = navigator.language;`. main.js:212 passes `locale: LOCALE`, which only customer-detail.js:132 takes. Commit 6e0f818 changed order-view.js and left line 199 as it was.","proven":true},
{"id":"CON-35","class":"contract","severity":"advisory","file":"src/ui/views/order-view.js","line":194,"what_breaks":"F-35 is reported closed by commits 6e0f818 and eba225d, but only the listeners of order-view.js changed. Views still take one context object holding the whole mutable state, they write state directly, and other views keep per-control listeners.","requirement":"none","rule":"JS-11","evidence":"ADR-003 line 35: 'A view has the shape `render(container, viewModel, actions)` and one delegated listener per container'. Code: order-view.js:194 `export function renderOrderView(container, context)`, :195 destructures `state`, :251 `state.form = { hash: location.hash, ...`. customer-form.js:119 and order-form.js:210 do the same. customer-detail.js:145 and :154 and customer-list.js:65 and :73 attach per-button listeners. F-35's text names all three parts: context object, listeners, direct writes to state.","proven":true},
{"id":"CON-36","class":"contract","severity":"advisory","file":"src/ui/main.js","line":100,"what_breaks":"F-43 is half closed. Deleting a customer clears the customer search but not the order search. R-04 tells the user to delete the orders first, and the natural way to find them is typing the customer's name into Search orders, so that name stays in the box after the customer's data is erased.","requirement":"R-04","evidence":"Cycle 1 LEG-1: 'with no reset of state.searchCustomers or state.searchOrders'. F-43: 'the same reset eraseAll does would close the gap'. Code: main.js:100 resets only `state.searchCustomers`; eraseAll at main.js:181-182 resets both; order-list.js:96 `input.value = state.searchOrders;` restores the text. R-04: 'deleting those orders (R-08) and then the customer erases all of this customer's data'.","proven":true},
{"id":"CON-37","class":"contract","severity":"advisory","file":"src/ui/format.js","line":17,"what_breaks":"The F-39 fix still does not follow the decision: formatDate never calls Date.UTC. The rewrite also adds handling and a test for years 0000 to 0099, inputs the human rejected as not real in F-29, so this is behaviour nothing asks for.","requirement":"none","evidence":"ADR-007 line 45: 'built with `Date.UTC` and formatted with `timeZone: 'UTC'`'. Code: format.js:17-18 `const date = new Date(0); date.setUTCFullYear(year, month - 1, day);`. tests/format.test.js:33 `R-28 formatDate shows 0099-01-01 as year 99`. docs/review/1/decisions.json note: 'F-29: years 0000 to 0099 are not a real input.' The shown day is right for every real date.","proven":true},
{"id":"CON-38","class":"contract","severity":"advisory","file":"tests/format.test.js","line":34,"what_breaks":"The assertion cannot catch the defect its title names. If formatDate used Date.UTC, year 99 would become 1999, and '1 Jan 1999' still includes '99'. Advisory because the test's other line can fail and the input is one the human ruled out in F-29.","requirement":"R-28","rule":"TS-05","evidence":"Test title: 'R-28 formatDate shows 0099-01-01 as year 99'. Assertion: `assert.equal(formatDate('0099-01-01', 'en-GB').includes('99'), true);`. Date.UTC maps years 0 to 99 onto 1900 to 1999, the reason dates.js:9 calls setUTCFullYear. AGENTS.md rule 2: 'A test must be able to fail'. Replacing format.js:17-18 with `new Date(Date.UTC(year, month - 1, day))` passes this assertion.","proven":true},
{"id":"CON-39","class":"contract","severity":"advisory","file":"tests/export.test.js","line":17,"what_breaks":"F-32 is half closed. The S3 half was fixed, but the S6 half is unchanged: the builder's export test still checks fragments of A-13 and A-14, and tests/export.test.js is in no fix commit. Only the tester's spec holds the full texts.","requirement":"R-29","rule":"TS-02","evidence":"PLAN line 164: `R-29 buildCustomerExport states the purpose of A-13, the retention of A-14 and the currency EUR`. Code: export.test.js:19 `assert.ok(result.purpose.endsWith('The data is used for nothing else.'));`, :20 `assert.ok(result.retention.includes('there is no fixed period'));`. F-32: 'the export test checks only fragments of A-13 and A-14'. F-32 was routed to S3 only, whose Files line does not hold this test. tests/export.spec.mjs:77-92 hold the stronger checks.","proven":true},
{"id":"CON-40","class":"contract","severity":"advisory","file":"tests/storage.test.js","line":16,"what_breaks":"Two builder tests assert a value that the empty default already gives. The R-19 round trip would pass if save wrote nothing, because load of an empty backing returns the same object. The R-06 erase test never raises the counter, so it proves no restart. Advisory because other tests catch both defects (storage.test.js:68 and the specs).","requirement":"R-19","rule":"TS-05","evidence":"tests/storage.test.js:14 `const data = { nextOrderNumber: 1, customers: [], orders: [] };`, :21 `assert.deepEqual(createStorage(backing).load(), { ok: true, data });`; storage.js:6 and :40 return that value for a missing key. tests/storage.test.js:46-50: `createStorage(memory())`, then `assert.equal(storage.erase().data.nextOrderNumber, 1);`. PLAN lines 182 and 199 name a saved-data round trip and a restart. tests/storage.spec.mjs:79 and :532 use real documents.","proven":true},
{"id":"CON-41","class":"contract","severity":"advisory","file":"docs/MANUAL-CHECKS.md","line":63,"what_breaks":"The R-01 clause added after review (a kept search is cleared on create) has no test and no manual check, the same gap F-44 closed for R-31. Nothing would catch a regression. The same holds for the F-43 clearing after a customer delete.","requirement":"R-01","evidence":"R-01: 'a customer search kept from before is cleared so the new customer is visible (review F-07)'. Code exists at main.js:100, which cannot run under Node (ADR-001). MANUAL-CHECKS.md:63 and PLAN line 342: 'save a name only, the customer appears in the list; save with email ab.c, the error shows and nothing is saved', with no search step. Grep for 'cleared' and 'search kept' in both files finds no such line. AGENTS.md Definition of done: 'listed for a manual check (UI)'.","proven":true},
{"id":"CON-42","class":"contract","severity":"advisory","file":"tests/validation.test.js","line":186,"what_breaks":"The invisible-text rule lives in R-17, but its tests carry R-01 and R-11, so a trace of R-17 misses it. The plan's S2 Tests first list was not updated for the new criterion, and the fix commit does not name R-17.","requirement":"R-17","rule":"TS-02","evidence":"R-17: 'A text made only of invisible characters (zero-width or other format characters) counts as empty for every required field (review F-13).' Tests: validation.test.js:186 `R-01 a customer name made only of invisible characters...`, :193 `R-11 a line description made only of invisible characters...`. AGENTS.md rule 4: 'Every requirement you implement is named in a test title'. Commit 4791fde: 'S2: fix F-03, F-13 (R-01, R-11)'. PLAN S2 Tests first (lines 43-58) has no such title.","proven":true},
{"id":"CON-43","class":"contract","severity":"advisory","file":"src/ui/views/order-form.js","line":85,"what_breaks":"On order edit the read-only Number field is labelled `Number (optional)`. This is the same complaint the human raised in UAT on the read-only Customer field, and the fix covered Customer only. Read 1: F-47 applies to every fixed value, so the label must lose the suffix. Read 2: the approved spec row gives Required 'no', so `(optional)` follows the spec.","requirement":"none","evidence":"decisions.json F-47: 'the label must say Customer and not call a fixed value optional'. Code: order-form.js:85-91 `field({ id: 'order-number', label: 'Number', required: false, ...`, and components.js:76 appends ' (optional)'. Only the customer label is overwritten, at order-form.js:75. UI-SPEC line 83: label 'with ` (required)` or ` (optional)` as part of the label text'; line 354: Number, Required `no`. Settled by the human saying whether F-47 covers Number.","proven":false},
